    "party_profiles": {
      "_doc": "BALANCE 3's standard 'party of tier T' (DEV: --raid-profile=<T> --raid-fort=<fort_id>, RaidLogic.profile_seed): what the risk targets and the dungeon stand-ins assume the player brings to a fort. garrison_units are the player's undead already at the fort's walls (chaff at garrison.stat_mult); starter_units are the first dungeon's only (0 here); party is one big undead per entry, stats as the slab rolls them (the pre_vei fixture's four bigs run power 3.4-8.8, beef 1.7-5.5, speed 3.7-7.6). Each tier adds a big and grows the stats; tier 2's big just meets both weak points (beef 6 braces the Bellringer, speed 4 intercepts the Huntsman). The fort holds living = cap * profile_living_frac (the start's realm start_living_frac) and dead = cap * profile_dead_frac; no phylactery charge. Fixed before calibration: tune the dungeon to the party, not the party to the targets.",
